# Required reviewers per path. Gitignore syntax; the LAST matching rule wins, so
# put the narrowest rules last.
#
# Covers the one gap CI cannot: a merge to `main` that rewrites the workflows
# themselves. → docs/decisions/000-ci-security-gates.md
#
# SHIPPED INERT. An entry naming an unresolvable user is silently ignored by
# GitHub, so a plausible-looking broken file is worse than an empty one.
#
# TODO(template) To activate, all three are required:
#   1. Replace @OWNER with a user or @org/team that has write access.
#   2. Branch protection → tick "Require review from Code Owners".
#   3. Open a PR touching .github/ and confirm the owner is auto-requested.
#
# Leave it commented if you cannot do step 2 — no branch protection (403 on a
# private free-plan repo), or you are the sole owner (nobody can approve their
# own PR, so the requirement is either a deadlock or a bypass). A second person
# with write access is what makes this file mean something.

# *                        @OWNER

# Paths where a self-merge rewrites what every other check asserts.
# /.github/                @OWNER
# /.githooks/              @OWNER
# /CODEOWNERS              @OWNER
# /.github/CODEOWNERS      @OWNER
# /docs/decisions/         @OWNER
